(6203462, 915547, 113156, '<td valign="top">One of my favorites so far, really nice shot, and i bet you had a lovely day out.</td>', 'One of my favorites so far, really nice shot, and i bet you had a lovely day out.', '2010-10-28 11:02:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(6203512, 916084, 85430, '<td valign="top">beautiful image. i like the brown background. It complements the bird. Perfect focus. With respect to the challenge, I think this was an easy and safe option to meet it. Birds don''t frown, nor squint under the sun. They don''t get panda eyes. This is a very beautiful photo, with lots of technical merit. But it doesn''t show how you were able to overcome the challenge of taking a photo of a subject under harsh daylight because birds really look good under any type of daylight.<br/> <br/>Outside the context of the challenge, i really like this photo.</td>', 'beautiful image. i like the brown background. It complements the bird. Perfect focus. With respect to the challenge, I think this was an easy and safe option to meet it. Birds don''t frown, nor squint under the sun. They don''t get panda eyes. This is a very beautiful photo, with lots of technical merit. But it doesn''t show how you were able to overcome the challenge of taking a photo of a subject under harsh daylight because birds really look good under any type of daylight. Outside the context of the challenge, i really like this photo.', '2010-10-28 12:39:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(6203522, 916051, 85430, '<td valign="top">I like how the light touches the leaves. I like the blurred background. I think the trunk of the tree may have occupied a very large area that doesn''t seem to add much to the image. I would have cropped it out and give emphasis to the leaves and how the sun shines on them.</td>', 'I like how the light touches the leaves. I like the blurred background. I think the trunk of the tree may have occupied a very large area that doesn''t seem to add much to the image. I would have cropped it out and give emphasis to the leaves and how the sun shines on them.', '2010-10-28 12:46:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(6203528, 916106, 85430, '<td valign="top">Very peaceful scenery. After a hard day''s work, I feel that my eyes have rested for a while after looking at this photo. The calmness of the water, the perfect blue sky, the color of the leaves and branches, and the silhouette of a man sitting by a bench perfectly suggest tranquility.</td>', 'Very peaceful scenery. After a hard day''s work, I feel that my eyes have rested for a while after looking at this photo. The calmness of the water, the perfect blue sky, the color of the leaves and branches, and the silhouette of a man sitting by a bench perfectly suggest tranquility.', '2010-10-28 12:52:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(6203537, 915781, 85430, '<td valign="top">Very harsh midday lighting indeed on the wall. But i think the challenge suggest that we not only show midday light, but how we overcame it as well. Compensating exposure for the very bright wall is one way to show that you were trying to beat the harsh midday sunlight, but that wasn''t done here.<br/> <br/>The lower left side of the margin was off by a few pixels.</td>', 'Very harsh midday lighting indeed on the wall. But i think the challenge suggest that we not only show midday light, but how we overcame it as well. Compensating exposure for the very bright wall is one way to show that you were trying to beat the harsh midday sunlight, but that wasn''t done here. The lower left side of the margin was off by a few pixels.', '2010-10-28 13:01:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(6203546, 915631, 85430, '<td valign="top">I would describe this photo as a very nicely executed snapshot. And i think it''s perfect for the challenge. <br/> <br/>What i like about this photo so much is that it shows the realism of the situation. I mean if i were a professional photographer, why would i shoot during midday outdoor? I''d rather wait for a better sunlight. But the reality is, most camera owners aren''t professional photographers who shoot artistic architectural photography. Some are tourists taking snapshots of places they went to. Some are just regular people who happen to be in a nice photo-worthy location during midday, and they happen to have brought along their camera. These people are the ones faced with the challenge of taking good snapshots during harsh midday sunlight. These people taking snapshots during midday should learn a thing or two from this photo.</td>', 'I would describe this photo as a very nicely executed snapshot. And i think it''s perfect for the challenge.  What i like about this photo so much is that it shows the realism of the situation. I mean if i were a professional photographer, why would i shoot during midday outdoor? I''d rather wait for a better sunlight. But the reality is, most camera owners aren''t professional photographers who shoot artistic architectural photography. Some are tourists taking snapshots of places they went to. Some are just regular people who happen to be in a nice photo-worthy location during midday, and they happen to have brought along their camera. These people are the ones faced with the challenge of taking good snapshots during harsh midday sunlight. These people taking snapshots during midday should learn a thing or two from this photo.', '2010-10-28 13:16:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(6203547, 915595, 85430, '<td valign="top">Rule of thirds nicely applied. I was wondering if there were more angles tried during framing of this shot. I mean, granted that there was room for you to move around, was it possible to find an angle that puts the tree on the left third of the photo and the fountain on the right third. That would have been great. But this one was also good.</td>', 'Rule of thirds nicely applied. I was wondering if there were more angles tried during framing of this shot. I mean, granted that there was room for you to move around, was it possible to find an angle that puts the tree on the left third of the photo and the fountain on the right third. That would have been great. But this one was also good.', '2010-10-28 13:21:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(6203548, 915760, 85430, '<td valign="top">Finally, after voting on more than ten images, this is the first one i saw with people as part of the subject. For me this is a good take on the challenge. There is no risk in taking photo of nature, buildings, and other large objects outdoor under a harsh midday light. But when you put faces of people in the frame, that''s where the challenge begins. How do you counter the harshness of the sunlight being thrown on a person''s face -- that''s what this challenge was all about. And i think this photo successfully overcomes that challenge.</td>', 'Finally, after voting on more than ten images, this is the first one i saw with people as part of the subject. For me this is a good take on the challenge. There is no risk in taking photo of nature, buildings, and other large objects outdoor under a harsh midday light. But when you put faces of people in the frame, that''s where the challenge begins. How do you counter the harshness of the sunlight being thrown on a person''s face -- that''s what this challenge was all about. And i think this photo successfully overcomes that challenge.', '2010-10-28 13:26:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(6203551, 916496, 85430, '<td valign="top">Very nice blue on the sea and the sky. The placement of the bush in the frame was also nicely done. What i don''t like in this image is the very bright sand. You may have interpreted the challenge as simply as to take a photo during midday, so that''s why the blown out highlights in the sand. To me, the wording on the challenge tells me to take a photo during midday and "overcome" the harsh light. One way to overcome that is to compensate for exposure of the bright areas and fill for the shadows. I believe that was not done here.</td>', 'Very nice blue on the sea and the sky. The placement of the bush in the frame was also nicely done. What i don''t like in this image is the very bright sand. You may have interpreted the challenge as simply as to take a photo during midday, so that''s why the blown out highlights in the sand. To me, the wording on the challenge tells me to take a photo during midday and "overcome" the harsh light. One way to overcome that is to compensate for exposure of the bright areas and fill for the shadows. I believe that was not done here.', '2010-10-28 13:33:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(6203557, 916163, 85430, '<td valign="top">Embracing the harsh daylight. Instead of dwelling on the negative effects of midday sunlight, why not explore the positive things that it brings. It produces strong, dramatic shadows. Photographed correctly, shadows tell a lot of story in a photo. This shot is perpect example of how you were able to beat the challenge of midday sunlight. Well done.</td>', 'Embracing the harsh daylight. Instead of dwelling on the negative effects of midday sunlight, why not explore the positive things that it brings. It produces strong, dramatic shadows. Photographed correctly, shadows tell a lot of story in a photo. This shot is perpect example of how you were able to beat the challenge of midday sunlight. Well done.', '2010-10-28 13:40:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(6203558, 916354, 57447, '<td valign="top">Looks like a great place for photos.  Nice foreground/background composition.</td>', 'Looks like a great place for photos.  Nice foreground/background composition.', '2010-10-28 13:42:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(6203575, 916480, 83313, '<td valign="top">Wasn''t that the title of a recent Dr. Who episode? Pretty scary enemies. Yours looks rather tame.</td>', 'Wasn''t that the title of a recent Dr. Who episode? Pretty scary enemies. Yours looks rather tame.', '2010-10-28 14:09:08.000000', NULL, 1),
