(6213333, 916084, 108069, '<td valign="top">You are a very accomplished photographer and you''ve put out some truly amazing stuff... but... as wonderful as this is, and it is, it''s not a harsh-sun shot.<b> I''ll be the ass in the room.</b> This has nothing to do with harsh, midday sun. Great shot, yes. Stole a ribbon from someone who shot for the challenge, yes.</td>', 'You are a very accomplished photographer and you''ve put out some truly amazing stuff... but... as wonderful as this is, and it is, it''s not a harsh-sun shot. I''ll be the ass in the room. This has nothing to do with harsh, midday sun. Great shot, yes. Stole a ribbon from someone who shot for the challenge, yes.', '2010-11-05 22:04:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(6213370, 916496, 107867, '<td valign="top">These happen to be my FAVorite 3 colors!!!!!!! :-)<br/>Thanks for sharing!!</td>', 'These happen to be my FAVorite 3 colors!!!!!!! :-)Thanks for sharing!!', '2010-11-05 23:00:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(6213545, 916084, 106109, '<td valign="top">Scott-<br/> <br/>I am sorry that you are so bitter. This photo was shot in mid day and under bright sun. It was also verified by DPChallenge as a legal edit. I followed the same ruled as everyone else. You can see a small hot spot on the neck and you can easily see the shadow on the end of the stick.<br/> <br/>Perhaps you require some anger management counseling?<br/> <br/>--Rick</td>', 'Scott- I am sorry that you are so bitter. This photo was shot in mid day and under bright sun. It was also verified by DPChallenge as a legal edit. I followed the same ruled as everyone else. You can see a small hot spot on the neck and you can easily see the shadow on the end of the stick. Perhaps you require some anger management counseling? --Rick', '2010-11-06 05:54:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(6213547, 916084, 56502, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by bohemka:</b></div><hr/><i> ... it''s not a harsh-sun shot.<b> I''ll be the ass in the room.</b> This has nothing to do with harsh, midday sun. Great shot, yes. Stole a ribbon from someone who shot for the challenge, yes. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>I''d like to disagree. Looking at the shadows the sun is pretty much from above. Looking at the exif-info it says: 2010:10:22 12:48:27. So it''s certainly around mid day (provided the clock in the camera is more or less correct). <br/> <br/>Great shot that well deserves its placement.</td>', 'Originally posted by bohemka: ... it''s not a harsh-sun shot. I''ll be the ass in the room. This has nothing to do with harsh, midday sun. Great shot, yes. Stole a ribbon from someone who shot for the challenge, yes.  I''d like to disagree. Looking at the shadows the sun is pretty much from above. Looking at the exif-info it says: 2010:10:22 12:48:27. So it''s certainly around mid day (provided the clock in the camera is more or less correct).  Great shot that well deserves its placement.', '2010-11-06 05:59:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(6213840, 916015, 116579, '<td valign="top">Thanks for good comments guys :)</td>', 'Thanks for good comments guys :)', '2010-11-06 14:41:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(6213926, 916203, 93565, '<td valign="top">This isn''t quite as insane as I thought it was going to be, what with your leadup lol.<br/>No worries, there was no way you''d know you''d get the ire of DPC pet haters.<br/>Getting lower for pet shots makes them feel more alive and interesting. Honestly though, the quality of the light isn''t so terrible for midday- pet coats can be a super PITA to keep from getting all sorts of blown highlights, and Copper was oriented in a fashion that he didn''t suffer from raccoon eye shadows or really dark and badly placed shadows.</td>', 'This isn''t quite as insane as I thought it was going to be, what with your leadup lol.No worries, there was no way you''d know you''d get the ire of DPC pet haters.Getting lower for pet shots makes them feel more alive and interesting. Honestly though, the quality of the light isn''t so terrible for midday- pet coats can be a super PITA to keep from getting all sorts of blown highlights, and Copper was oriented in a fashion that he didn''t suffer from raccoon eye shadows or really dark and badly placed shadows.', '2010-11-06 17:46:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(6214165, 916084, 76335, '<td valign="top">Totally valid as a midday shot, and as such, very impressive.</td>', 'Totally valid as a midday shot, and as such, very impressive.', '2010-11-06 23:12:07.000000', NULL, 0),
